findings.finding:
9 of 17 adversarial mutants of the delta survive the directed file and the whole 921-test suite. Seven are behaviour-relevant:
- QM31-02, -03 and -04: keep dropped on the eligibility, post-race and standing-route/RECOVERED early returns;
- QM31-05: rows declared after the decision clock are read;
- QM31-07: an early return keeps only the new row and drops the whole carried execution record; caught only by harness P10 on DEV-19;
- QM31-11: hash check removed; the tamper test is not its witness;
- QM31-17: a review with a template interruption reads the kept break.
QM31-08 and -09 are equivalent. The candidate behaves correctly on every path probed: 02, 03 and 04 record the break (qe31-persistence earlyReturns, qe31-post-race), 05 does not read a future-clock row, 07 keeps the record (P10 on DEV-19), 11 refuses an edited row (tamperedConsistentFacts; read on the mutant). The instruments do not detect P31-M5 (applied twice), P31-M6 (newer ignored), QM31-02, -04 or -11 on the dev cases.
